# P2-3 — Nsight Systems profiling window (2026-09-04).
# Delta overlay: sourced by tp4ctl, the launcher and scripts/deploy.sh AFTER cluster.env.
#
# The ENGINE FLAGS ARE THE PRODUCTION ONES, bit for bit: same CONTAINER, same
# MAX_MODEL_LEN, same SPEC_TOKENS, same EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS. This window is not a new lane —
# it adds only (a) the host Nsight Systems tree as a read-only mount (the image ships no
# nsys) and (b) an entrypoint wrapper that starts the engine under `nsys launch`.
#
# `nsys launch` merely attaches the profiler and opens the named session `tp4`; it
# collects nothing until `nsys start --session=tp4` runs. Steady-state serving is
# therefore the production one, and the profiling cost is confined to the explicit
# start/stop window driven by scripts/prof-capture.sh from the workstation.
#
# RESULTS land under ~/vllm-cache/profiles/ on the node (the container's /cache is the
# host ~/vllm-cache, persistent): the .nsys-rep survives the rollback restart.
#
# PREREQUISITE: scripts/deploy-host.sh must have pushed node/host/nsys-entry.sh to
# ~/tp4/host/ on every node (push phase only — no --run, this is not an --apply/--revert
# knob). scripts/deploy.sh pushes this overlay itself, to ~/tp4/experiments/.
#
# RUN THE PRECHECK, twice: `scripts/prof-capture.sh precheck` BEFORE the restart (a node
# missing the nsys tree makes that rank die and `tp4ctl up` hang for its full 35-min health
# timeout instead of failing fast) and AGAIN right after it (it re-verifies that PID 1 is
# nsys and that a Worker still carries LD_PRELOAD=/opt/patched-nccl through the re-exec).
#
# NOT PRODUCTION-COMPARABLE: CUPTI is attached for the whole life of the container, not
# just inside the start/stop window, and nsys-entry.sh sets --cuda-graph-trace=node (nsys
# warns of "significant runtime overhead") so decode kernels inside CUDA graphs are visible
# individually. Read the kernel MIX from this window; never quote its tok/s as a lane result.
#
# BEFORE ANY `tp4ctl down`/`restart`: `nsys stop --session=tp4`. PID 1 is nsys, and a
# collection still running at teardown can lose its report (prof-capture.sh traps on EXIT).
#
# ROLLBACK: ./tp4ctl restart with NO TP4_ENV (~22 min). Nothing on the node changed but
# two pushed files, both inert while no TP4_ENV names them.
# See experiments/README.md and node/host/README.md.

# Production value — KEEP IN SYNC with cluster.env. Repeated verbatim only because an
# overlay that redefines nothing else must not silently drop it.
EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS="--kv-cache-memory=17179869184 --moe-backend triton"

# SINGLE-quoted on purpose: the launcher expands a leading $HOME in every `-v` source
# ON THE NODE (expand_home() in launch-glm53-tp4.sh), so the value must not be expanded
# here. `--entrypoint` accepts one executable with no arguments, hence the wrapper.
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV='-v /opt/nvidia/nsight-systems:/opt/nvidia/nsight-systems:ro -v $HOME/tp4/host/nsys-entry.sh:/nsys-entry.sh:ro --entrypoint /nsys-entry.sh'
